[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2827866170","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105711#issuecomment-2827866170","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105711","id":2827866170,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ojdA6","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-24T14:31:24Z","updated_at":"2025-04-24T14:35:14Z","body":"Seems fine as a quick fix as I don't think this will be a very common use case either way.\r\n\r\nBut in theory I think it could be possible to use OpenXR + Wayland + Vulkan and compile out Godot's OpenGL3 / Compatibility rendering driver/method (which is what the `opengl3` option is meant to control, not only whether we can use libGL/libEGL). An EGL context would still be needed, so that's somewhat related to OpenGL, but (a priori, didn't check) it shouldn't be necessary to have our full-blown compatibility renderer for that?\r\n\r\nWe could check how the current Wayland display driver uses EGL + Vulkan when OpenGL is compiled out.\r\n\r\n*Edit:* Well `platform/linuxbsd/wayland/egl_manager_wayland.h` also is guarded by `GLES3_ENABLED`, so nevermind, currently we don't support EGL without our Compatibility renderer. Not sure what happens when building with `wayland=yes opengl3=no` then, is it usable?\r\n\r\nCC @Riteo","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2827866170/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2827944676","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105711#issuecomment-2827944676","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105711","id":2827944676,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ojwLk","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-24T14:56:21Z","updated_at":"2025-04-24T14:56:21Z","body":"> Not sure what happens when building with `wayland=yes opengl3=no` then, is it usable?\r\n\r\nIt seems to work!\r\n\r\nI logged out, switched to Wayland, ran a simple XR project (using Monado's QWERTY driver, which is like a simulator), and from the output it seems to be using both Wayland and Vulkan:\r\n\r\n```\r\ndsnopek@thelio:~/Sync/Projects/games/XR Template (main *)$ ~/prj/default/godot-4/bin/godot.linuxbsd.editor.dev.x86_64 --rendering-method mobile --display-driver wayland\r\nGodot Engine v4.5.dev.custom_build.dc380f891 (2025-04-24 14:17:19 UTC) - https://godotengine.org\r\nOpenXR: Running on OpenXR runtime:  Monado(XRT) by Collabora et al 'GIT-NOTFOUND'   21.0.0\r\nWARNING: Can't obtain the XDG decoration manager. Libdecor will be used for drawing CSDs, if available.\r\n     at: init (platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp:4262)\r\nOpenXR: XrGraphicsRequirementsVulkan2KHR:\r\n - minApiVersionSupported:  1.0.0\r\n - maxApiVersionSupported:  1023.1023.1023\r\nWARNING: GENERAL - Message Id Number: 0 | Message Id Name: Loader Message\r\n        terminator_CreateInstance: Received return code -3 from call to vkCreateInstance in ICD /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libvulkan_virtio.so. Skipping this driver.\r\n        Objects - 1\r\n                Object[0] - VK_OBJECT_TYPE_INSTANCE, Handle 94841486580064\r\n     at: _debug_messenger_callback (drivers/vulkan/rendering_context_driver_vulkan.cpp:639)\r\nVulkan 1.3.280 - Forward Mobile - Using Device #0: NVIDIA - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti\r\n```\r\n\r\nEverything worked through Monado as expected","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2827944676/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2828215222","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105711#issuecomment-2828215222","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105711","id":2828215222,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6okyO2","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-24T16:30:19Z","updated_at":"2025-04-24T16:30:19Z","body":"Welp looks like the issue has already been figured out :P\r\n\r\nI'll just add that I've very quickly glanced over the docs and it indeed looks like OpenXR does not depend on any specific API per-se, as it can piggy-back whatever is available through special extensions. So yeah, I'm sure that we're good :D","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2828215222/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2828992178","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105711#issuecomment-2828992178","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105711","id":2828992178,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6onv6y","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubuse